engine.robust_np restates villa's normalize_robust and engine.hann2d villa's floored Hann blend map (both MIT,
Copyright (c) Vesuvius Challenge) so the batched device version can be checked against them. Apart from the ink-sdk
rules restated below, Ink Lens copies no other third-party code. When it starts, it downloads the following at
pinned versions and uses them under their own licenses, which still apply:

- villa's vesuvius package, https://github.com/ScrollPrize/villa at commit
  8aa507c1215f1fa8758f13d0538f7af9710e02d7: MIT License, Copyright (c) Vesuvius Challenge.
- d9v2_ft-012000.pth, https://github.com/TAUIL-Abd-Elilah/pherc0826-first-letters-search release v1.0:
  MIT License, Copyright (c) TAUIL-Abd-Elilah. A fine-tune of ink_9um.
- scrollprize/ink_9um hybrid_3d2d-seed42/step-075000.pth, https://huggingface.co/scrollprize/ink_9um: MIT License,
  Copyright (c) Vesuvius Challenge.

The model comparison (zoo.py, runners.py, compare.py, tools/gallery_job.py) restates ink-sdk's liveness thresholds,
its ensemble input mapping and its depth-window and scale rules (compare._assess_local, compare.map_values,
runners.window, zoo.scale_plan; ink-sdk, https://github.com/LimeGS/ink-sdk, MIT License, Copyright (c) LimeGS), so
they hold when ink-sdk is absent and can be checked against it. It installs ink-sdk at commit
1dbfac2178958ca4bca7469582477963d4d08ecf and runs its Hecate and canonical adapters, liveness gate and orientation
check in process. It downloads, at the revisions and SHA-256 pinned in zoo.py, under their own licenses:

- scrollprize/ink_9um seeds 42 and 43, scrollprize/hecate (2.4 and 9.6 um), scrollprize/ink_canonical_2um,
  scrollprize/ink_paris4_3d_4.8um_gambiarra and scrollprize/ink_3d_dino_guided: MIT License, Copyright (c)
  Vesuvius Challenge.
- domenicor046/reader-v2 and domenicor046/reader-v3: MIT License, Copyright (c) Domenico Russo.
- Nieuwlaar/ink9um-dense-native: MIT License, Copyright (c) Erwin Nieuwlaar.

The gallery job (tools/gallery_job.py) runs the scan-space 3D models through AutoPipeline's kit ink3d (Apache License
2.0, same copyright as this file) and villa's infer_full3d_tifxyz and paris4_3d_gambiarra code (MIT, Copyright (c)
Vesuvius Challenge), fetched at pinned commits when the job runs.

The client's letter pins use the Scroll Text Reader (kit/letterread.py, Apache License 2.0) with the letters-v2-ccby
weights (CC BY 4.0; credits in docs/letter-reader.md of ChaseHendrick/Scrolls).

